   "id": "f29f3e8a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Slot 35: Graduate Presentations, Day 1\n",
    "\n",
    "**Format.**\n",
    "- A **presentation** and a **1-page written summary** that describes practical deployment of electrochemistry.\n",
    "    - Select a technology/electrochemical application and an important scientific parameter/metric for it\n",
    "    - Summarize experimental techniques that are used to study this parameter/metric\n",
    "    - Explicitly identify the assumptions (implicit and explicit) than underpin this measurements; discuss their reliability\n",
    "    - Identify common shortcomings in the literature: where are these assumptions ignored? What is the effect?\n",
    "- 20 minutes each: 15 minutes of talk, 5 minutes of questions.\n",
    "- Each presentation can be delivered by a team of 2. \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## For the presenters\n",
    "\n",
    "Graded on:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Criterion | Weight |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Written summary | 20% |\n",
    "| Scientific content and correctness | 30% |\n",
    "| Depth: does it go past a review-level summary? | 10% |\n",
    "| Clarity of explanation to a mixed-level audience | 20% |\n",
    "| Figures and slide preparation | 10% |\n",
    "| Handling of questions | 10% |\n",
    "\n",
    "## For everyone else\n",
    "\n",
    "You are not an audience, you are reviewers. Complete one peer-review sheet per talk and submit them at the end of the class. A rubric will be provided.\n"
   ]
  },
